From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:02:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: Let axi_daisy change at run time

The Daisy bridge tables are applied in avd_backend_boot(), at each
decoder power-up before the decoder CPU starts, and the bridge window
reads its reset values at that point (mode 2 on a fresh boot). The
parameter was 0444, so comparing the reset bridge with macOS's tables
took one boot per mode.

Make it 0644 and read it once per power-up. A value written while the
decoder is runtime-suspended takes effect at its next power-up, so one
boot can measure the decoder with and without the tables. The default
stays 0 (no access).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c | 13 +++++++------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
index 5e147254801..1003f248a72 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
@@ -350,15 +350,15 @@ void avd_pm_apply_axi_tunables(struct avd_dev *avd)
  * axi_tunables switch above writes another generation's (Tansy's)
  * values and is not used with this one.
  *
- * Boot-only test switch, read at each power-up before the decoder CPU
+ * Test switch, read once at each power-up before the decoder CPU
  * starts: 0 = no access (default), 1 = log every planned write and touch
  * nothing, 2 = read each register once and log it (an access to the
  * bridge window), 3 = program the tables in macOS's order.
  */
 static unsigned int axi_daisy;
-module_param(axi_daisy, uint, 0444);
+module_param(axi_daisy, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(axi_daisy,
-		 "Test only: T8132 bridge as macOS's Daisy: 0 off, 1 log only, 2 read, 3 program (boot only, default 0)");
+		 "Test only: T8132 bridge as macOS's Daisy: 0 off, 1 log only, 2 read, 3 program (read at each decoder power-up, default 0)");
 
 static const struct avd_tunable avd_daisy_flow_up[] = {
 	{ 0x0000, 0x800000ff, 0x80000026 }, /* UP_CMD_CREDIT_GS_ALLOC */
@@ -506,16 +506,17 @@ static void avd_pm_daisy_report(struct avd_dev *avd, const char *what,
 void avd_pm_apply_axi_daisy(struct avd_dev *avd)
 {
 	u32 before[ARRAY_SIZE(avd_daisy_flow_up) + ARRAY_SIZE(avd_daisy_flow_dn)];
+	unsigned int mode = READ_ONCE(axi_daisy);
 	unsigned int ok;
 
-	if (!axi_daisy || axi_daisy > 3 || !avd->pm.axi2af)
+	if (!mode || mode > 3 || !avd->pm.axi2af)
 		return;
 	if (READ_ONCE(axi_tunables)) {
 		dev_warn_ratelimited(avd->dev, "AXI daisy refused: axi_tunables is set\n");
 		return;
 	}
-	if (axi_daisy == 1 || axi_daisy == 2) {
-		void __iomem *base = axi_daisy == 2 ? avd->pm.axi2af : NULL;
+	if (mode == 1 || mode == 2) {
+		void __iomem *base = mode == 2 ? avd->pm.axi2af : NULL;
 
 		avd_pm_daisy_log(avd, "up", avd_daisy_flow_up,
 				 ARRAY_SIZE(avd_daisy_flow_up), base);
-- 
